#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "fd3cb5b1-f16e-5a52-82e4-25bbbd1c4fe7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4789" :question/problem "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/df62636427555a986454d8d2787e110eb664771f5a74a38fdaa99ec593643729.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119544 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "548ef945-392b-5e75-9b60-14f4e2de6261" :question/math-academy-id "e-4790" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/0e6491c477a442fc9dae1462413d593815a6761393ad3a0d2f8d72de665a7c93.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119545 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "13ebde04-8518-5837-9420-c9487debc562" :question/math-academy-id "e-4791" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/e9e0ea8fb6e9ba5f4595f15efe4f04e93db373dbc020f5672db34d5a3c12024b.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then what is $x_1+x_2?$" :question/worked-solution "If $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5,$ which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 4(5)+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(5)+(-15) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15,$ which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119593 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/id #uuid "d9beff9d-db58-540f-811e-a07fb77d3d92" :question/math-academy-id "e-6191" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/4749f1e50cf7768f39d26737bfce4d9e8e85d5b350f4bc9844a358cd4c3c5cc0.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/a4e5c5eba6d2d8b30955668d47bb2a131c702cc7ec62ef7dada9ed9ad60d8182.png)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "896ea9d6-d71a-55be-b137-a5e8ac75f68b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321255} {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b900c-9290-573e-8125-c6bec2f64905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321256} {:answer/id #uuid "1176f2ad-3206-5c46-9a89-46355b922602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321257} {:answer/id #uuid "4e4f0f10-e223-5ad9-92de-237ec6ada06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321258} {:answer/id #uuid "0ccb8b67-8dc0-5b12-86be-ddd6cb929af2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321259}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c1b900c-9290-573e-8125-c6bec2f64905" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321256} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a6f583-b3f7-5ed3-b22e-5a4039b73977" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a8f533b-003a-5522-aad6-99090100d40d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105152" :question/problem "Find $h$, if $3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $h$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+h{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ h[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $h=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89cc5e84-4859-5d7d-b94d-e1a19c84bae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321262} {:answer/id #uuid "5667f1d2-a6b7-572a-9fae-043899b206bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321263} {:answer/id #uuid "69cdf29b-e913-5e53-9ca7-34b79a399071" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321264} {:answer/id #uuid "1f301354-63d7-597b-94f8-fa2401e71bd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321265} {:answer/id #uuid "0096632c-9047-5f65-8938-f66a5c4683ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89cc5e84-4859-5d7d-b94d-e1a19c84bae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321262} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d7e98e5-76c6-5b42-ba31-10b23c39e729" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95b01bbb-b87e-5d85-a984-9a967436e82e" :question/math-academy-id "q-105154" :question/problem "Find $m$, if $7{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $m$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{a}_{1}+m{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 7[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+m[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ m[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]-7[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ m[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $m=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321267 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "539d4c37-cf3f-5deb-8522-02a759b1ba9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321269} {:answer/id #uuid "43e5c3b3-bbaf-51c8-8464-b39799ed8f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321270} {:answer/id #uuid "f5eded6c-b801-54f9-8be8-bc8c66e155b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321271} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d69ec1-746a-5a30-ab01-963040c12fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321272} {:answer/id #uuid "87c117b6-ca2d-55a7-8405-dd019cd72d85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7d69ec1-746a-5a30-ab01-963040c12fd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321272} :answer-field/id #uuid "adeed958-2c6b-5fda-b6cf-b5f268db8d10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ebd8d026-a8f0-5c49-8cd6-0d2ba4d731b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-105157" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $2a+4x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+4x & =b \\\\ 4x & =b-2a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}(b-2a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da3e8477-106a-521d-8a5d-9630a7bc7c26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321276} {:answer/id #uuid "cae62d13-13fa-5405-b9a6-0ed064c5201b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321277} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae4ddc5-b348-50fa-94e4-25334b8f929f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321278} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e83399-74df-5213-b06f-ff33cd0de475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321279} {:answer/id #uuid "44e79f27-17e0-5f99-8ba5-d097ce1b005c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1e83399-74df-5213-b06f-ff33cd0de475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321279} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d9dbf6e-96ba-5f6e-b3da-3fd310777917" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "60bf6437-ed03-5b91-94f9-bc6aaa385bd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-105159" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $4a+3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =b-4a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(b-4a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}([\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e07a459-22fe-5949-9f39-35f0dac3bced" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321283} {:answer/id #uuid "98d94017-7488-5d27-b458-c5f70ee69ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321284} {:answer/id #uuid "d1abdd28-119d-573a-b5f2-ef53c34d3a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321285} {:answer/id #uuid "5da4737e-684d-59fb-a7fa-6adb71845d00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321286} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0f82f4-6944-55e3-aabd-ccae112cfdc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98d94017-7488-5d27-b458-c5f70ee69ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321284} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0ba3eed-8266-55c1-807d-41fac73f44e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d9c5e6f-2efe-59f5-b686-ce41270ba17b" :question/math-academy-id "q-105166" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the resulting equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3(-5) & =1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & =-14 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 3(7)+5(-5) & =-4 \\\\ -4 & =-4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ which means\n\n$$\n7{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7+(-5)=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5961a60b-5c5e-536c-88f0-a957562f8c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321290} {:answer/id #uuid "97b19ab2-2796-5e89-9c51-610a26830c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321291} {:answer/id #uuid "3f88aeac-4bbe-57ac-be93-de9880bcdddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321292} {:answer/id #uuid "21659538-f832-5e08-ab59-38761bdee52c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321293} {:answer/id #uuid "4bfffae9-f4ff-5d51-ae85-e10337ef4213" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f88aeac-4bbe-57ac-be93-de9880bcdddc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321292} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2769ef7-8b4a-55db-86e7-1a9436610fa9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e791d02b-d07a-5985-aeae-67250de997e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-105172" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ -21{x}_{2} \\\\ -12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 14{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=18 \\\\ 0=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-1$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "382d93ad-2e02-5155-92da-be5439a4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321297} {:answer/id #uuid "7a5fc2fa-5f72-5ad0-8fd1-69aef1192d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321298} {:answer/id #uuid "1f5d0608-98d6-5575-8b82-82ab03f3b03c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321299} {:answer/id #uuid "f20cb265-08c1-578b-9e9d-7fea1f9cb223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321300} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9c0a5e-f0ac-5af4-9e4c-4aca14345995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "382d93ad-2e02-5155-92da-be5439a4d870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321297} :answer-field/id #uuid "e62db11a-3245-5286-acf2-e78cc28d847e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49d86e24-f480-5ade-b4df-5af4f350fca2" :question/math-academy-id "q-34242" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0=4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation is a false statement. Hence,the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120243 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "972a3fef-203d-572e-9899-5e0b2c6e0630" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117959} {:answer/id #uuid "a83599ad-2be5-5e43-b83a-069c19db8cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117960} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b2e220-aa44-53a1-8e91-1098cf158db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117961} {:answer/id #uuid "3896fd9b-3724-5e00-a5e0-7c3c15a1e476" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117962} {:answer/id #uuid "38cca5f0-0e27-56f5-a922-3d986adc2f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a83599ad-2be5-5e43-b83a-069c19db8cb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117960} :answer-field/id #uuid "16b82190-b4c3-5c75-a997-45752f71579f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac599c23-1c9e-5d96-a71a-974c272cf869" :question/math-academy-id "q-34248" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $4a+6x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+6x & =b \\\\ 6x & =b-4a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}(b-4a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}36 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120244 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9aa334b7-13cf-55a3-918a-f652cf01fad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117965} {:answer/id #uuid "a73ab8df-4a60-5d1e-bb5b-2e153c6a27f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117966} {:answer/id #uuid "2008a0f1-3e24-571f-8d93-fa0b11c91fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117967} {:answer/id #uuid "34c44a5d-3108-549d-8bd7-60bf918e4d02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117968} {:answer/id #uuid "52eb16ba-330e-52ff-9425-54d2a010e4bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9aa334b7-13cf-55a3-918a-f652cf01fad5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117965} :answer-field/id #uuid "a55c6b52-41b4-585b-9cd6-f8f47908d13e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117964}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4e441944-ad54-59d2-9897-793ac5452b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-34249" :question/problem "Find $l$, if $5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}45 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $l$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 5[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]+l[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}45 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}] \\\\ l[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}45 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}]-5[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ l[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $l=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120282 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba411921-937a-5ff2-b95c-2c2ab52d7f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118168} {:answer/id #uuid "fd01c1f2-324b-5abd-ac30-bfef1b81b856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118169} {:answer/id #uuid "06aeaafe-6358-5847-a39a-65e26880c857" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118170} {:answer/id #uuid "1887f5de-3296-5ad9-a0a7-651a3e2e8117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118171} {:answer/id #uuid "6218bbff-56c9-57cd-b302-1a6ec05e497b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6218bbff-56c9-57cd-b302-1a6ec05e497b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118172} :answer-field/id #uuid "dab07291-9c12-5e5c-b621-1a50ea481200" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "04e10334-4152-5cfe-aad7-249b23effb61" :question/math-academy-id "q-34566" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 0=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=13$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adbd15bc-996f-5fa8-8137-294ead5712ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321304} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3df985-2a43-5034-8407-967afbe23e81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321305} {:answer/id #uuid "3466eb65-6b99-5a87-86b3-d3e17b2716dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321306} {:answer/id #uuid "ffddc4ee-1c87-5d6a-8384-a42ed341d8a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321307} {:answer/id #uuid "b15877db-48d5-5313-9118-c76f1b0d213b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adbd15bc-996f-5fa8-8137-294ead5712ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321304} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f979f6-dff2-5bc8-8704-74077bb93426" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7f13166f-63f4-5f1f-b7d3-38f111dea761" :question/math-academy-id "q-34570" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n3k=-6\\,⟹\\,k=-2.\n$$\n\nBut then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that $3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33586620-e110-5a37-874f-a92103c5e9fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for One Coefficient in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec209f6-9f67-5be4-a1e5-a058b0c97e42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321311} {:answer/id #uuid "4cae1f17-e703-5cbd-b52f-ebdb2959db84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321312} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2abbb8-30d6-5419-81df-961c80bd67f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321313} {:answer/id #uuid "515df100-2311-55f6-84d3-5b2b3c2cddd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321314} {:answer/id #uuid "01273b43-df1c-5f5b-a6c8-eec678b2dff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cae1f17-e703-5cbd-b52f-ebdb2959db84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321312} :answer-field/id #uuid "94f49771-acfd-5c3a-aeaf-c2fd40d7b5b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aada095f-b604-55ca-adb1-bafdd7c5b85b" :question/math-academy-id "q-34602" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]+k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ k[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get \n\n$$\n-2k=24\\,⟹\\,k=-12.\n$$\n\nBut then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -36 \\\\ 48\\end{aligned}]\\ne [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 32\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that \n $8{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321316 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "240d5547-f75a-5217-a337-31ed278a378b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321318} {:answer/id #uuid "8334a2a9-9569-515a-8062-f982ee8c163c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321319} {:answer/id #uuid "31d57cf9-5e7a-5f99-8bef-908e67dea7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321320} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4282fc-1a7a-5917-896a-a286112f6957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321321} {:answer/id #uuid "d30c39d8-471d-5cb9-9a9a-5833d6fddc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31d57cf9-5e7a-5f99-8bef-908e67dea7ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321320} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3022814-08a0-5872-9a60-95a62167c0ed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8eb567c3-b45a-5792-98ad-b502b4836a87" :question/math-academy-id "q-73931" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $3a+2x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-3a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-3a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321323 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "590953b8-2533-5a4b-bf4f-f002b0367919" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Vector in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0249a497-0690-5a90-abdc-53b8ebf2b945" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321325} {:answer/id #uuid "86df16d6-95e1-5a1d-a4a3-fde60d9267b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -15 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321326} {:answer/id #uuid "e779c6c8-4f3e-5e92-a76e-37d624eca5a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321327} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e7384b-50f2-574b-8289-63e799e8a3f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321328} {:answer/id #uuid "15f07c39-69e1-5e4c-a645-b0eb07e6ccc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e779c6c8-4f3e-5e92-a76e-37d624eca5a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321327} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3048bc4-7714-50ab-935a-5840286d87fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "23c4b644-31d0-50c4-9b7b-4910d79509cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73933" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $5a-3x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5a-3x & =b \\\\ 3x & =5a-b \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(5a-b) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(5[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -48 \\\\ 51\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -16 \\\\ 17\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29475f1b-ddc2-5713-a560-ff80acf114a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321332} {:answer/id #uuid "feec4427-c165-5d44-850a-f46341050c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321333} {:answer/id #uuid "279fa3c9-cd8e-53ce-bcf5-08f02de7d37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321334} {:answer/id #uuid "82e88e8d-cabf-599f-abaa-d031639540b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321335} {:answer/id #uuid "125e02f4-7360-5425-9504-fbee83158e4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feec4427-c165-5d44-850a-f46341050c72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321333} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c395a36-ec62-59c1-ab1e-9dee4bd9949b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c4aa4d92-2f8e-50b3-bd53-f6e46489ca0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73951" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d9e1e9a2-153d-517b-ab67-7837c2168555" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321339} {:answer/id #uuid "ed1b1e93-7840-5a85-a773-ae87f2b5dd73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321340} {:answer/id #uuid "49de6bee-41ab-548b-bd49-2d7003a678e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321341} {:answer/id #uuid "c9dc09a7-17e3-52a0-b09e-3b562d4778e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321342} {:answer/id #uuid "e027474a-a491-5523-a95b-98e263653e6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49de6bee-41ab-548b-bd49-2d7003a678e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321341} :answer-field/id #uuid "b90369b5-0596-5750-b1d1-222b297e0373" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "49280f22-8d86-589c-8580-452aa67d8a42" :question/math-academy-id "q-73952" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equation we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(4) & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-7+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =6 \\\\ 2(-3)+3(4) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+4=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "92e5e826-3121-500a-9103-e618cb16c5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Two Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c2ccb57-0437-54c6-9855-a2610fd49379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321346} {:answer/id #uuid "6d0541eb-e8aa-5d80-9118-889d57922dff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321347} {:answer/id #uuid "ed643955-12da-56fb-9053-884113c63ada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321348} {:answer/id #uuid "f7aac712-7a95-53f0-9bd2-ee5de29e3a08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321349} {:answer/id #uuid "897f5f15-af76-5632-8189-2cbdcd7de4a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d0541eb-e8aa-5d80-9118-889d57922dff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321347} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0e912b-229b-5e03-8456-7a5a57eb8965" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321345}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df8a5f4e-332d-5630-99c3-186e9e92363a" :question/math-academy-id "q-73981" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the third equation by $-1$ and adding the result to the first equation we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{1} & =7-4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow,  we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ into the third equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 3(3)-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ -{x}_{2} & =4-9 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ -2(3)+3(5) & =9 \\\\ -6+15 & =9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5,$ which means\n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+5=8.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b51b8540-8251-593e-bb7c-7866c6982b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321353} {:answer/id #uuid "16fdf2e2-347b-59af-b07c-24062400f72f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321354} {:answer/id #uuid "b3e7c73c-42b2-55d7-ad1c-c77f7404ce8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321355} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef91dd2-1ac2-5f46-a7b7-71c807c82724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321356} {:answer/id #uuid "19de8df7-505e-56ad-9e7c-9dc5f9f4489c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b51b8540-8251-593e-bb7c-7866c6982b49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321353} :answer-field/id #uuid "062c5f1d-4b8e-51b9-a5e2-07c1a9cdf07e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321352}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0bd5d095-8bad-5d93-a96b-8e2c28877938" :question/math-academy-id "q-74028" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2,{x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(-1) & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-5 & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means \n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4+(-2)-(-1)=3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321358 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbc964ce-7179-5d39-90b8-63ab4b6a71b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321360} {:answer/id #uuid "b95f7d8c-a8d1-5fdc-8f38-7bb4d379a4e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321361} {:answer/id #uuid "5f2fd9b2-0430-5909-bccb-e8612211f708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321362} {:answer/id #uuid "467e0bdc-9778-54b0-9938-f8de39e30cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321363} {:answer/id #uuid "fa89ef78-78f6-58cb-bf66-1f98d6d9f97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa89ef78-78f6-58cb-bf66-1f98d6d9f97a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321364} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4413af7-ca5e-52fa-8023-3a23c164b23e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321359}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54baa5a4-47af-54e2-a17a-a1381c32da92" :question/math-academy-id "q-74032" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3}=-18 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -15 & -30\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{15}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this value into  the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(2)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(2) & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=1$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2,$ which means \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-2)+2=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "13a44dc8-4699-519f-8cb1-87ad77471ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ed0055d-a5be-5df9-8104-2f7390a936c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321367} {:answer/id #uuid "5dd10ed7-3869-50da-99f6-054698d6a187" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321368} {:answer/id #uuid "06ebd8bc-353f-59a5-9d60-6b6e6162f828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321369} {:answer/id #uuid "b902bf8f-e56e-512e-969d-fa2952b73f43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321370} {:answer/id #uuid "4036b2c7-1a54-5e6e-b55b-0de6b3104351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ed0055d-a5be-5df9-8104-2f7390a936c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321367} :answer-field/id #uuid "e00b97b3-26f0-5556-be44-84b3e6f4f24c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3b211c6a-15ea-5e7f-9d6a-b8b7c7ba9865" :question/math-academy-id "q-74046" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=5.$ Substituting this value in the second and first equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{2}-2(5)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{1}+5=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=5,$ which means \n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+4+5=12.\n$$"}]}
